    "id": "rate_half_bivariate_single_coefficient_rational_interpolation_criterion",
    "title": "Single-coefficient rational-interpolation criterion",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "dual Reed-Solomon kernel characterization",
    "statement": "Let n=|W|, s=4m+1 and r=n-s. The two-block matrix with columns (x^i)_i and (h(x)x^i)_i has full column rank exactly when there are no polynomials 0!=P,Q of degrees below r satisfying Q(x)=h(x)P(x) on W. If the unique O=0 deficient point x_0 lies in W and its lower clone is included, the same criterion holds with agreement required only on W minus {x_0}. For the bivariate j=m block, h_m(x)=-(mu_x+sum_(gamma in A_x)gamma). At m=2 this differs by a constant from the third-root datum nu_x. The criterion is exact but does not exclude the rational certificate.",
